.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt BRFSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm brfsd
.Nd BrFS replication daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl config Ns = Ns Ar path
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl Fl help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
daemon replicates a local directory tree between members of a BrFS
replication group, DFSR-style: multi-master, last-writer-wins with
deterministic (origin_seq, node_id) tiebreak, losers quarantined under
.Pa state_dir/conflicts/ .
.Pp
.Nm
consumes the change feed of the
.Xr brfs 4
kernel module (the ONLY change-detection path; there is no inotify
fallback), maintains the content set in LMDB under
.Pa state_dir/csdb ,
and exchanges framed binary messages with every other member over a full
mesh (PSK-authenticated HELLO; TLS 1.3 with KTLS offload and DANE
TLSA-first validation when
.Va tls_cert / Va tls_key
are configured).
.Pp
The kernel module must be loaded before
.Nm
starts; the supplied rc script refuses to start otherwise.
Only one
.Nm
may run per kernel
.Pq Pa /dev/brfs
is single-open.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--config=path"
.It Fl Fl config Ns = Ns Ar path
Configuration file (UCL).
Default:
.Pa /usr/local/etc/brfs.conf .
See
.Xr brfs.conf 5 .
.It Fl h | Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGTERM"
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload the configuration (runtime reconfig).
Reloadable without restart: the PSK (re-read from
.Va psk_file ;
applies to new handshakes), the peer list (NEW addresses get outbound
dials; existing connections are untouched, and peer REMOVAL requires a
restart), and
.Va rate_limit .
Changes to identity/topology fields
.Pq Va node_id , replicated_path , state_dir , listen , primary , tls_*
are logged as warnings and ignored.
A reload that fails to parse keeps the running configuration.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Clean shutdown: completion-worker drain, content-set checkpoint, watch
root removal.
.El
.Sh SAFETY BEHAVIOUR
.Bl -tag -width "Mass-delete guard"
.It Em Mass-delete guard
When local deletes cross BOTH an absolute floor (64) AND half the live
tree inside a 10-second window, the guard latches: local deletes stop
becoming tombstones, so an accidental
.Ic rm -rf
of the replicated tree does not propagate mesh-wide.
Release with
.Ic brfsctl massdelete resume ,
which schedules a rescan that re-derives the suppressed deletes as honest
tombstones (an intentional delete still converges, one confirmation
later).
Incoming peer tombstones are never suppressed.
.It Em Staging free-space precondition
A fetch whose announced size does not fit the staging filesystem's
available bytes (f_bavail) minus a 64 MiB reserve is refused BEFORE any
bytes are staged; the fetch retries on the next announce/resync round.
The reserve also covers the content-set env and the conflicts directory,
which share the filesystem.
.It Em Forced-unmount freeze
The content set is married to the replicated root's filesystem id
(stamped on first start).
If the watched filesystem is force-unmounted (or rebuilt), the path
resolves to the wrong filesystem and the daemon freezes — no scans, no
local announces, no watch re-push — rather than tombstoning the
apparently vanished tree mesh-wide.
Restore the mount and restart
.Nm ;
wipe
.Pa state_dir
only if the filesystem was legitimately rebuilt.
A non-forced
.Xr umount 8
of a watched filesystem fails
.Er EBUSY
(the kernel module holds a reference).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/brfsd.sock"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/brfs.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /var/db/brfs/
Default state directory: content set
.Pq csdb/ ,
staging area
.Pq staging/ ,
conflict quarantine
.Pq conflicts/ .
.It Pa /var/run/brfsd.sock
Operator control socket (mode 0600), consumed by
.Xr brfsctl 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brfs 4 ,
.Xr brfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr brfsctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
daemon first appeared in the BrFS POC in August 2026.
